les:\n\tsubfile\n\nnothing added to commit but untracked files present\n```\n\nEdit:  Here's `git log --stat` in ds:\n\n```\n% git log --stat\ncommit 3465dbb9fa9ac34e1d13a6d3f52453699133db78 (HEAD -\u003e master)\nAuthor: Kyle Meyer \u003ckyle@kyleam.com\u003e\nDate:   Mon Feb 4 14:37:03 2019 -0500\n\n    [DATALAD] Recorded changes\n\n d1/subds/subfile | 0\n file             | 0\n 2 files changed, 0 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1549310067,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2MDM4ODQxMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3139#issuecomment-460388412"},"message":"True, I will investigate.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1549310067,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE4MDAzNjIxMQ=="},"target":"8731e91704d4f9a539fea0618f31021938fc11be780fcab9240fe3f531da7573","message":"True, I will investigate. Still surprising, as it is based on:\n\n```\n% datalad rev-status *\nuntracked: d1 (directory)\nuntracked: file (file)\n```","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1549346978,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50MjExNzYwNDE2Mg=="},"added":[],"removed":["fixed-in-revolution"]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1549351872,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2MDUzOTI5Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3139#issuecomment-460539292"},"message":"Update: The -revolution failure is due to the specifics of bug demo code. It uses empty repositories (without a single commit) that obviously cannot be added to a superdataset. With datasets it behaves as expected. I will adjust the code to foresee this possibility.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1549354119,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2MDU0MjY0Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3139#issuecomment-460542647"},"message":"The reason for the actual failure (in -revolution) is that `git ls-files` does not treat repos without an initial commit like repos with a commit.\n\nStarting from the same original state of the test above:\n```\n% git ls-files --stage -d -m --exclude-standard -o\nd1/subrepo/subfile\nfile.txt\n100644 b540820107ca5718dc0f196a08edf3729239bfef 0       .datalad/.gitattributes\n100644 7ab9c7d6877fac805d76818b07e7a3e35fa1cc12 0       .datalad/config\n100644 c3aaefef9a2470b31ba9213350046ff7cde75737 0       .gitattributes\n\n% git -C d1/subrepo add subfile\n% git -C d1/subrepo commit -m first\n% git ls-files --stage -d -m --exclude-standard -o\nd1/subrepo/\nfile.txt\n100644 b540820107ca5718dc0f196a08edf3729239bfef 0       .datalad/.gitattributes\n100644 7ab9c7d6877fac805d76818b07e7a3e35fa1cc12 0       .datalad/config\n100644 c3aaefef9a2470b31ba9213350046ff7cde75737 0       .gitattributes\n```\n\nNote how the file is present in the first output, but only the repo is present in the second one. This is precisely the test condition that is used in -revolution to detect subdataset without expensive tests.\n\n*IF* we would want to support users placing empty non-dataset repositories inside dataset and not have them be ignored (like `ls-files`), but treated as subdatasets (which they are not), then we will have to test all parent directories of any untracked file for evidence of a repository root. Once found, we would then ignore such repository and all files therein. Unfortunately, this is a relatively expensive test, as it will have to happen on an expanded list of untracked files, in any repository, regardless of whether there is a subrepository or not.\n\nGiven this assessment, I personally think it is best to document that such scenario is not supported.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1549354119,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE4MDI0ODExOA=="},"target":"4599690b6a9777c2ca080782a2b298eae31e3a3fb6f42c1157691ab56dd3b7f4","message":"The reason for the actual failure (in -revolution) is that `git ls-files` does not treat repos without an initial commit like repos with a commit.\n\nStarting from the same original state of the test above:\n```\n% git ls-files --stage -d -m --exclude-standard -o\nd1/subrepo/subfile\nfile.txt\n100644 b540820107ca5718dc0f196a08edf3729239bfef 0       .datalad/.gitattributes\n100644 7ab9c7d6877fac805d76818b07e7a3e35fa1cc12 0       .datalad/config\n100644 c3aaefef9a2470b31ba9213350046ff7cde75737 0       .gitattributes\n\n% git -C d1/subrepo add subfile\n% git -C d1/subrepo commit -m first\n% git ls-files --stage -d -m --exclude-standard -o\nd1/subrepo/\nfile.txt\n100644 b540820107ca5718dc0f196a08edf3729239bfef 0       .datalad/.gitattributes\n100644 7ab9c7d6877fac805d76818b07e7a3e35fa1cc12 0       .datalad/config\n100644 c3aaefef9a2470b31ba9213350046ff7cde75737 0       .gitattributes\n```\n\nNote how the file is present in the first output, but only the repo is present in the second one. This is precisely the test condition that is used in -revolution to detect subdataset without expensive tests.\n\n*IF* we would want to support users placing empty non-dataset repositories inside dataset and not have them be ignored (like `ls-files`), but treated as subdatasets (which they are not), then we will have to test all parent directories of any untracked file for evidence of a repository root. Once found, we would then ignore such repository and all files therein. Unfortunately, this is a relatively expensive test, as it will have to happen on an expanded list of untracked files, in any repository, regardless of whether there is a subrepository or not.\n\nGiven this assessment, I personally think it is best to document that such scenario is not supported.\n\nGit itself seems to make a similar assessment of this situation:\n\n````\nmih@meiner /tmp % mkdir ds \u0026\u0026 cd ds \u0026\u0026 git init \u0026\u0026 touch file \u0026\u0026 mkdir -p d1/subds \u0026\u0026 git -C d1/subds init \u0026\u0026 touch d1/subds/subfile \u0026\u0026 git add *\nInitialized empty Git repository in /tmp/ds/.git/\nInitialized empty Git repository in /tmp/ds/d1/subds/.git/\nmih@meiner /tmp/ds (git)-[master] % git status\nOn branch master\n\nNo commits yet\n\nChanges to be committed:\n  (use \"git rm --cached \u003cfile\u003e...\" to unstage)\n\n        new file:   d1/subds/subfile\n        new file:   file\n````","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1549354144,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE4MDI0ODIwNw=="},"target":"4599690b6a9777c2ca080782a2b298eae31e3a3fb6f42c1157691ab56dd3b7f4","message":"The reason for the actual \"failure\" (in -revolution) is that `git ls-files` does not treat repos without an initial commit like repos with a commit.\n\nStarting from the same original state of the test above:\n```\n% git ls-files --stage -d -m --exclude-standard -o\nd1/subrepo/subfile\nfile.txt\n100644 b540820107ca5718dc0f196a08edf3729239bfef 0       .datalad/.gitattributes\n100644 7ab9c7d6877fac805d76818b07e7a3e35fa1cc12 0       .datalad/config\n100644 c3aaefef9a2470b31ba9213350046ff7cde75737 0       .gitattributes\n\n% git -C d1/subrepo add subfile\n% git -C d1/subrepo commit -m first\n% git ls-files --stage -d -m --exclude-standard -o\nd1/subrepo/\nfile.txt\n100644 b540820107ca5718dc0f196a08edf3729239bfef 0       .datalad/.gitattributes\n100644 7ab9c7d6877fac805d76818b07e7a3e35fa1cc12 0       .datalad/config\n100644 c3aaefef9a2470b31ba9213350046ff7cde75737 0       .gitattributes\n```\n\nNote how the file is present in the first output, but only the repo is present in the second one. This is precisely the test condition that is used in -revolution to detect subdataset without expensive tests.\n\n*IF* we would want to support users placing empty non-dataset repositories inside dataset and not have them be ignored (like `ls-files`), but treated as subdatasets (which they are not), then we will have to test all parent directories of any untracked file for evidence of a repository root. Once found, we would then ignore such repository and all files therein. Unfortunately, this is a relatively expensive test, as it will have to happen on an expanded list of untracked files, in any repository, regardless of whether there is a subrepository or not.\n\nGiven this assessment, I personally think it is best to document that such scenario is not supported.\n\nGit itself seems to make a similar assessment of this situation:\n\n````\nmih@meiner /tmp % mkdir ds \u0026\u0026 cd ds \u0026\u0026 git init \u0026\u0026 touch file \u0026\u0026 mkdir -p d1/subds \u0026\u0026 git -C d1/subds init \u0026\u0026 touch d1/subds/subfile \u0026\u0026 git add *\nInitialized empty Git repository in /tmp/ds/.git/\nInitialized empty Git repository in /tmp/ds/d1/subds/.git/\nmih@meiner /tmp/ds (git)-[master] % git status\nOn branch master\n\nNo commits yet\n\nChanges to be committed:\n  (use \"git rm --cached \u003cfile\u003e...\" to unstage)\n\n        new file:   d1/subds/subfile\n        new file:   file\n````","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1549389436,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2MDczODQ3OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3139#issuecomment-460738479"},"message":"\u003e Given this assessment, I personally think it is best to document that such scenario is not supported.\n\nSounds sensible to me.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1549393051,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2MDc1OTU3Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3139#issuecomment-460759572"},"message":"\u003e Given this assessment, I personally think it is best to document that such scenario is not supported.\n\nI am ok to not support such scenario even though would be a blow to our pride imho while claiming that the mighty datalad works across repositories boundaries etc.\nBut it is not merely a documentation issue. If not supported, we must either blow (exception) when we run into such case (e.g., while annotating paths) with some informative instruction (\"make a commit in repo X or make it into a proper datalad dataset\") or issue a warning with similar message and then ignore any related path.  DataLad must not perform incorrect operation (adding file into super repo ignoring present .git in subrepo).","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1549393051,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE4MDUyMTYzMg=="},"target":"e8a2b793a3246cad78fe62a4f29d61ba6ce6e1be42b331aeb38cb1b770b666ed","message":"\u003e Given this assessment, I personally think it is best to document that such scenario is not supported.\n\nI am ok to not support such scenario even though it would be a little blow to our pride when we claim that the mighty DataLad works across repositories boundaries etc (but fails on such an easy from user's perspective case).\nBut it is not merely a documentation issue. If not supported, we must either blow (exception) when we run into such case (e.g., while annotating paths?) with some informative instruction (\"make a commit in repo X or make it into a proper datalad dataset\") or issue a warning with similar message and then ignore any related path.  \nDataLad must not perform incorrect operation (adding file into super repo ignoring present .git in subrepo).","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1549437840,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2MDkyNTExNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3139#issuecomment-460925115"},"message":"My point was that the detection of such a case is the expensive part -- without detection there is no error reporting. This cost would need to be paid unconditionally. DataLad works perfectly fine across dataset boundaries (which is what it should care about). It even works fine across repository boundaries, for everything that Git itself acknowledges as a repository to consider in this context. Supporting more than that comes with little real-world benefit, and guaranteed costs.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1554853143,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4MTQ3OTEwOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3139#issuecomment-481479109"},"message":"I think we can consider this closed given that there are [patches] to address this upstream.  With a little luck, those should land and `git ls-files` will start listing repos without an initial commit in the same way as it lists other repos.\n\nOnce that makes it into a release, I'll update the note in rev-save's help and test_surprise_subds accordingly.\n\n[patches]: https://public-inbox.org/git/20190409230737.26809-1-kyle@kyleam.com","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1554853144,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjI2NDUwNzIxOA=="},"status":2},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1554853928,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDIyNjQ1MjQ2MjM="},"added":["external-tools"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1554853938,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50MjI2NDUyNDg2MQ=="},"added":[],"removed":["severity-normal"]}]}